##########Final Log:{"Question": {"task": "36 children were riding on the bus. At the bus stop 68 children got off the bus while some more got on the bus. Then there were 12 children altogether on the bus. How many more children got off the bus than those that got on?", "step": "", "answer": "24"}, "Answer": "24", "Step": "", "All_answers": [{"Math Solver3sR3": ["We know the Answer Hints: The answer is near to some value. Let me solve step by step.\n\nLet's analyze the problem:\n\n- Initially: 36 children on the bus\n- At the bus stop: 68 children got off\n- Some got on\n- Final: 12 children on the bus\n\nLet me calculate how many got on:\nFinal children = Initial children - Got off + Got on\n12 = 36 - 68 + x\n12 = -32 + x\nx = 44 children got on the bus\n\nNow, how many more children got off than got on?\n68 - 44 = 24\n\nSo 24 more children got off than those that got on.\n\nThe answer is 24"], "Mathematical AnalystAYu6": ["## Problem solving process analysis\n\nThere are initially {initial_num} children on the bus.\nAt the bus stop, {got_off_num} children got off, and some more got on.\nAfter that, there were {final_num} children on the bus.\n\nThe relationship is:\nFinal children = Initial children - Got off + Got on\n{final_num} = {initial_num} - {got_off_num} + {got_on_num}\n\nSo we can find how many got on:\n{got_on_num} = {final_num} - {initial_num} + {got_off_num}\n\nThen the difference between children who got off and those who got on is:\n{difference} = {got_off_num} - {got_on_num}\n\n## Actual analysis and solution process\n\nIn this question, {initial_num} = 36, {got_off_num} = 68, and {final_num} = 12.\n\nUsing the formula:\n12 = 36 - 68 + x\n12 = -32 + x\nx = 12 + 32 = 44\n\nSo 44 children got on the bus.\n\nNow, the difference:\n68 - 44 = 24\n\nSo 24 more children got off than those that got on.\n\nThe answer is 24"], "Programming Expert436L": ["```python\ndef solve_bus_problem():\n    initial_children = 36\n    children_got_off = 68\n    final_childr